course: dictionary
lesson: 10751
title: Urgent: needing action now
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Urgent means very important and needing to be done straight away. «Never go anywhere with someone you don't know, however urgent or scary their story.» Even when a stranger seems to be in a hurry, you do not go with them. The word urgent tells you the story is pressing, but it does not make it safe.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Phone calls are best made between about 9 in the morning and 8 in the evening, unless it is urgent.» The word unless tells you that urgent is the exception: an urgent call can be made at any time. Try your meaning in the sentence: "unless it is very important and needs doing straight away" still makes sense.
explain: Urgent can also describe a voice or a look. An urgent voice shows that someone needs something quickly. «When it is urgent, like someone being hurt, you interrupt straight away.» Here urgent means serious enough that you must not wait.
fact: Urgent means very important and needing to be done or dealt with straight away.
fact: «Urgent help», «urgent message» and «it's urgent» are common phrases.
fact: An urgent message must be read at once.
fact: «Urgent» can describe a voice or look that shows someone needs something quickly.
fact: In 2022 UNESCO listed Ukrainian borshch cooking as heritage in need of urgent protection, meaning it needed protecting soon.
exercise: «Never go anywhere with someone you don't know, however urgent or scary their story.» What does urgent mean here? | Very funny and silly | *Needing attention straight away | Lost in the rain | Very quiet and calm
exercise: «Phone calls are best made between about 9 in the morning and 8 in the evening, unless it is urgent.» What does unless it is urgent mean? | Unless it is a Tuesday | Unless it is very long | *Unless it is very important and needs doing at once
exercise: Ella reads «It's urgent» on a note from school. What should she do? | *Read it straight away | Leave it until next week | Use it as a bookmark
test: An urgent message must be read at once. What does at once mean? | Never | Next month | *Straight away | Only if you feel like it
test: Which situation is most urgent? | A library book is a week late | Your bedroom needs tidying | You want a new pencil case | *Someone is not breathing
exam: Jayden says, «Urgent» means late. Is he right? | Yes, urgent means late and nothing else | *No, urgent means very important and needs doing straight away | Yes, urgent means slow and boring
